  "description": "Unapproved cap1 draft of A(a), B(b), C(c) in their single original number-line frame. Modern regularization: straight strokes, readable Latin labels and a wider A-B gap than B-C; all coordinate magnitudes are layout-only. SOURCE HOLD: damage crosses the A marker, so its original fill state cannot be established from this one source view. The default modern A point glyph records presence and location only and is not a source-fill determination. No invented origin, numerical tick, or coordinate value.",
